[2026-03-16T01:34:55.826Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PK5ZkdjS6wuYoHEb4jifwc","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution history. As stated, \"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe system uses two main types of points in recordings:\n- **Points**: Specific execution moments when JS statements run or significant events occur\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of particular points\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline tracking (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (listing, reading, and searching source files)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Dependency analysis showing cause-effect relationships\n- Point details including variable values and component trees\n- Expression evaluation at specific moments\n\n## Best Practices\n\nThe document emphasizes a structured investigative approach: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before exploring data systematically. For understanding timing issues, use the ControlDependency tool to \"explore the events that had to happen first and any associated delays.\"\n\nThe Logpoint tool is particularly valuable for tracking expression values across multiple executions and identifying unexpected behavior patterns."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3335dc11-543c-4527-b006-a5422834d5f8","uuid":"87ba03d9-74cf-40d8-b4fa-0be5411fc00d","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution history. As stated, \"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe system uses two main types of points in recordings:\n- **Points**: Specific execution moments when JS statements run or significant events occur\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of particular points\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline tracking (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (listing, reading, and searching source files)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Dependency analysis showing cause-effect relationships\n- Point details including variable values and component trees\n- Expression evaluation at specific moments\n\n## Best Practices\n\nThe document emphasizes a structured investigative approach: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before exploring data systematically. For understanding timing issues, use the ControlDependency tool to \"explore the events that had to happen first and any associated delays.\"\n\nThe Logpoint tool is particularly valuable for tracking expression values across multiple executions and identifying unexpected behavior patterns.","durationMs":3372,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-16T01:34:55.883Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013c8aPnW3i4QdQfBw2r5Yq7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings through command-line interface.\n\n## Key Installation Method\nUsers can install globally via: `npm i -g replayio` (with yarn, pnpm, and bun alternatives available)\n\n## Authentication Setup\nUsers must navigate to the Replay.io settings page, generate an API key, and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Essential Commands\n\n**Recording:** `replayio record [url]` - \"Launches Replay Browser and starts recording the given URL\"\n\n**Uploading:** `replayio upload [ids...]` - \"Uploads one or more recordings\" and returns a viewable URL\n\n**Management:** \n- `replayio list` - displays all local recordings with ID, host, date, duration, and status\n- `replayio remove [ids...]` - removes one or more recordings\n- `replayio login/logout` - authentication management\n\n**Utilities:**\n- `replayio info` - shows installed dependency and version information\n- `replayio update` - updates the Replay Browser component\n- `replayio upload-source-maps` - uploads source maps with grouping and filtering options\n\n## Standard Workflow\n1. Record a session: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. Upload the recording (manually if needed): `replayio upload <recording-id>`\n3. Optionally integrate MCP server for debugging within Claude\n\nAll commands support `-h` or `--help` flags for detailed information."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3335dc11-543c-4527-b006-a5422834d5f8","uuid":"58d77398-84a2-4839-924c-102264cb02b4","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings through command-line interface.\n\n## Key Installation Method\nUsers can install globally via: `npm i -g replayio` (with yarn, pnpm, and bun alternatives available)\n\n## Authentication Setup\nUsers must navigate to the Replay.io settings page, generate an API key, and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Essential Commands\n\n**Recording:** `replayio record [url]` - \"Launches Replay Browser and starts recording the given URL\"\n\n**Uploading:** `replayio upload [ids...]` - \"Uploads one or more recordings\" and returns a viewable URL\n\n**Management:** \n- `replayio list` - displays all local recordings with ID, host, date, duration, and status\n- `replayio remove [ids...]` - removes one or more recordings\n- `replayio login/logout` - authentication management\n\n**Utilities:**\n- `replayio info` - shows installed dependency and version information\n- `replayio update` - updates the Replay Browser component\n- `replayio upload-source-maps` - uploads source maps with grouping and filtering options\n\n## Standard Workflow\n1. Record a session: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. Upload the recording (manually if needed): `replayio upload <recording-id>`\n3. Optionally integrate MCP server for debugging within Claude\n\nAll commands support `-h` or `--help` flags for detailed information.","durationMs":3937,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
